  "output": "Now I have a complete picture of the codebase. Here is the full analysis:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis\n\n### 1. Critical: Domain Lock Held During Sleep (`engine.py:79–84`)\n\n**Issue:** The `_domain_lock` is acquired, sleep happens while holding it, then released. This serializes *all* domain requests while any single domain waits its 1-second rate limit.\n\n```python\n# Current — blocks every domain while one sleeps\nasync with self._domain_lock:\n    delay_required = 1.0 - (time.time() - last_request)\n    if delay_required > 0:\n        await asyncio.sleep(delay_required)   # ← holds the global lock\n    self._domain_last_request[domain] = time.time()\n```\n\n**Fix:** Separate the read-then-update into atomic operations; release the lock before sleeping.\n\n```python\nasync def _fetch_with_concurrency(self, url: str) -> str:\n    domain = self._get_domain(url)\n\n    async with self._domain_lock:\n        last_request = self._domain_last_request[domain]\n        self._domain_last_request[domain] = time.time()   # optimistic write\n\n    delay = 1.0 - (time.time() - last_request)\n    if delay > 0:\n        await asyncio.sleep(delay)           # lock NOT held\n\n    async with self._domain_semaphores[domain]:\n        return await self._do_fetch(url)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Critical: Cache Check After Acquiring Semaphores (`engine.py:61–65, 89–95`)\n\n**Issue:** Cache is checked *inside* `_do_fetch`, which is called *after* acquiring both the global semaphore (10 slots) and domain semaphore (3 slots). Cached hits waste concurrency capacity.\n\n```python\n# Current: semaphores held → then cache checked\nasync def fetch(self, url):\n    async with self._global_semaphore:          # acquired\n        return await self._fetch_with_concurrency(url)\n        # ...which acquires domain semaphore...\n        # ...which calls _do_fetch...\n        # ...which THEN checks cache\n```\n\n**Fix:** Check cache first, before touching semaphores.\n\n```python\nasync def fetch(self, url: str) -> str:\n    url = self._normalize_url(url)\n    cached = await self._cache.get(url)         # check first, no semaphore needed\n    if cached is not None:\n        return cached.content\n    async with self._global_semaphore:\n        return await self._fetch_with_concurrency(url)\n\nasync def _do_fetch(self, url: str) -> str:\n    # Remove cache check from here — already done in fetch()\n    try:\n        response = await self._client.get(url)\n        ...\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. High: No Database Connection Pooling (`db.py`)\n\n**Issue:** Every method calls `aiosqlite.connect(self._db_path)` as a fresh connection. A single query invokes ~15+ DB operations (save query, 8 agent responses, orchestrator response, feedback read…). Each open/close cycle includes file locking and journal setup overhead.\n\n```python\n# Current — new connection on every call\nasync def save_query(self, record):\n    async with aiosqlite.connect(self._db_path) as db:   # opened\n        await db.execute(...)\n        await db.commit()\n    # closed immediately\n```\n\n**Fix:** Hold a persistent connection opened at `initialize()` time.\n\n```python\nclass DatabaseManager:\n    def __init__(self, db_path=_DB_PATH):\n        self._db_path = db_path\n        self._db_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        self._db: aiosqlite.Connection | None = None\n\n    async def initialize(self) -> None:\n        self._db = await aiosqlite.connect(self._db_path)\n        self._db.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n        await self._db.executescript(_SCHEMA)\n        await self._db.commit()\n\n    async def close(self) -> None:\n        if self._db:\n            await self._db.close()\n\n    async def save_query(self, record):\n        await self._db.execute(\"INSERT OR REPLACE INTO queries ...\", (...))\n        await self._db.commit()\n```\n\nAlso add an index — `agents_invoked` is stored as JSON text but queried by `query_id` which already has a PK. The `agent_responses` table is queried with `WHERE query_id = ?` and would benefit from an index:\n\n```sql\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_agent_responses_query_id ON agent_responses(query_id);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_orchestrator_responses_query_id ON orchestrator_responses(query_id);\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. High: Policy Registry Read N Times (`specialist.py:72–75`)\n\n**Issue:** `_load_instruments()` opens and parses `policy_registry.json` once per `SpecialistAgent.__init__` — called 8 times at startup.\n\n```python\ndef _load_instruments(self, agent_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n    with open(_REGISTRY_PATH) as f:        # disk read, JSON parse × 8\n        registry = json.load(f)\n    return [r for r in registry if agent_id in r[\"agent_ids\"]]\n```\n\n**Fix:** Cache the full registry at module level.\n\n```python\n_REGISTRY: list[dict] | None = None\n\ndef _get_registry() -> list[dict]:\n    global _REGISTRY\n    if _REGISTRY is None:\n        with open(_REGISTRY_PATH) as f:\n            _REGISTRY = json.load(f)\n    return _REGISTRY\n\nclass SpecialistAgent(GenericAgent):\n    def _load_instruments(self, agent_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n        return [r for r in _get_registry() if agent_id in r[\"agent_ids\"]]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. High: Gemini `GenerativeModel` Recreated on Every Call (`llm/client.py:40–50, 70–76`)\n\n**Issue:** `chat()`, `stream_chat()`, and `chat_parsed()` each call `self._make_model()`, which creates a new `genai.GenerativeModel` object every time. This incurs object construction and config dict creation for every LLM call (dozens per query).\n\n```python\nasync def chat(self, system_prompt, user_message, model=None):\n    m = self._make_model(model)   # ← new object every call\n    ...\n```\n\n**Fix:** Cache models keyed by `(model_name, json_output)`.\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self):\n    ...\n    self._model_cache: dict[tuple[str, bool], genai.GenerativeModel] = {}\n\ndef _make_model(self, model: str | None = None, json_output: bool = False) -> genai.GenerativeModel:\n    key = (model or self._model_name, json_output)\n    if key not in self._model_cache:\n        generation_config = {\n            \"temperature\": self._config.model.temperature,\n            \"top_p\": self._config.model.top_p,\n        }\n        if json_output:\n            generation_config[\"response_mime_type\"] = \"application/json\"\n        self._model_cache[key] = genai.GenerativeModel(\n            model_name=key[0],\n            generation_config=generation_config,\n        )\n    return self._model_cache[key]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Medium: `content_hash` Recomputes SHA-256 on Every Access (`cache.py:37–38`)\n\n**Issue:** `content_hash` is a `@property` that hashes the full content string (up to 48 KB) every time it is accessed.\n\n```python\n@property\ndef content_hash(self) -> str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(self.content.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()  # ← recomputed\n```\n\n**Fix:** Compute once using `__post_init__` (since this is a `@dataclass`).\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass CacheEntry:\n    url: str\n    content: str\n    ttl_hours: int\n    status_code: int | None = None\n    content_length: int | None = None\n    _content_hash: str = field(default=\"\", init=False, repr=False)\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        self._content_hash = hashlib.sha256(self.content.encode()).hexdigest()\n\n    @property\n    def content_hash(self) -> str:\n        return self._content_hash\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Medium: Regex Recompiled on Every Fetch (`engine.py:68–72`)\n\n**Issue:** `_normalize_url` does `import re` and compiles a regex pattern inline on every call.\n\n```python\ndef _normalize_url(self, url: str) -> str:\n    import re                                                    # ← imported every call\n    if re.search(r'laws-lois\\.justice\\.gc\\.ca/eng/acts/[^/]+/$', url):\n```\n\n**Fix:** Module-level compiled pattern.\n\n```python\nimport re\n\n_LAWS_ACT_RE = re.compile(r'laws-lois\\.justice\\.gc\\.ca/eng/acts/[^/]+/$')\n\nclass FetchEngine:\n    def _normalize_url(self, url: str) -> str:\n        if _LAWS_ACT_RE.search(url):\n            return url.rstrip('/') + '/FullText.html'\n        return url\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. Medium: DOM Query on Every Streaming Chunk (`app.js:172–183`)\n\n**Issue:** `handleResponseChunk()` queries the DOM each time a chunk arrives. For streaming responses this can be called hundreds of times.\n\n```javascript\nfunction handleResponseChunk(data) {\n    let messageEl = chatHistory.querySelector('.message.system:last-of-type');  // ← DOM search every chunk\n    ...\n    textEl.textContent += data.chunk;   // also triggers reflow each time\n```\n\n**Fix:** Hold a reference to the active system message element.\n\n```javascript\nlet activeSystemMessage = null;   // module-level alongside currentQueryId\n\nfunction handleResponseChunk(data) {\n    if (!activeSystemMessage) {\n        activeSystemMessage = createMessage('system', '', currentQueryId);\n        chatHistory.appendChild(activeSystemMessage);\n    }\n    const textEl = activeSystemMessage.querySelector('.message-text');\n    textEl.textContent += data.chunk;\n    scrollToBottom();\n}\n\nfunction resetProcessingState() {\n    currentQueryId = null;\n    activeSystemMessage = null;   // clear on reset\n    ...\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. Medium: Potential Catastrophic Backtracking in Citation Regex (`app.js:482–493`)\n\n**Issue:** `wrapWithCitations()` builds a regex with `[\\s\\S]*?` (which is dotAll). For long response text and many citations this can be very slow, and the pattern `(prefix[\\s\\S]*?)` is a greedy/lazy alternation that can exhibit worst-case O(n²) behavior.\n\n```javascript\nresult = result.replace(\n    new RegExp(`(${search.replace(...)}[\\\\s\\\\S]*?)`, 'gi'),  // ← hazardous on large text\n    `$1${marker}`\n);\n```\n\nAdditionally, this function is called from `updateMessageWithMetadata()` which is never invoked in the main code path — it's dead code in the current flow. **Consider removing it or rewriting it using simple `indexOf` + string slicing if needed.**\n\n---\n\n### 10. Low: Duplicate Agent Name Maps (`app.js`)\n\nThree separate objects mapping agent IDs to display names exist: `AGENT_DISPLAY_NAMES` (line 22), `agentNames` inside `renderCitations` (line 332), and `badgeNames` inside `updateMessageWithMetadata` (line 296).\n\n**Fix:** Use `AGENT_DISPLAY_NAMES` as the single source and reference it in both functions.\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| # | Location | Type | Severity | Impact |\n|---|----------|------|----------|--------|\n| 1 | `engine.py:79` | Concurrency bug — lock held during sleep | **Critical** | Serializes all fetches during rate-limit delays |\n| 2 | `engine.py:61,89` | Cache miss path holds semaphores | **Critical** | Wastes all 10 global + 3 domain concurrency slots on cache hits |\n| 3 | `db.py` | No connection pooling | **High** | 15+ connection open/close per query |\n| 4 | `specialist.py:72` | JSON file read ×8 at startup | **High** | 8× disk I/O and JSON parse at startup |\n| 5 | `llm/client.py:40` | `GenerativeModel` recreated per call | **High** | Object alloc + config dict on every LLM call |\n| 6 | `cache.py:38` | SHA-256 recomputed on every property access | **Medium** | CPU waste proportional to content size |\n| 7 | `engine.py:69` | `import re` + regex compile per fetch | **Medium** | Module import + regex compile on every URL |\n| 8 | `app.js:172` | DOM query per streaming chunk | **Medium** | Layout recalc × number of chunks |\n| 9 | `app.js:486` | Catastrophic backtracking regex | **Medium** | O(n²) string scan; also dead code |\n| 10 | `app.js:332` | 3× duplicate agent name maps | **Low** | Maintenance burden |\n\nThe three critical/high items in the fetch engine and database layer will have the most visible runtime impact — fixing them will reduce per-query latency meaningfully, since each query currently serializes all domain fetches and opens up to 15+ SQLite connections.\n",
